menu "Gantry application"

    config GANTRY_SELFTEST
        bool "Enable on-target selftest console command"
        default y
        help
            When enabled, the interactive serial console exposes the
            "selftest" command, which runs runBasicTests() (kinematics,
            joint-limit, and trajectory sanity checks) directly on the target.

            The same assertions also run host-side in CI (test/host/), so a
            production build can set this to "n" to drop both the "selftest"
            command and the basic_tests.cpp source from the firmware without
            losing test coverage.

    config GANTRY_SUPPRESS_GEOMETRY_WARNING
        bool "Suppress dev-rig geometry compile reminder"
        default n
        help
            axis_drivetrain_params.h emits a #warning when gantry geometric
            offsets are still development-rig placeholders. ESP-IDF v6 treats
            that as a build error (-Werror=cpp).

            Enable this for CI or bring-up builds that knowingly use unfrozen
            geometry. Local developer builds should leave this disabled so the
            one-time reminder in main.cpp stays visible.

            Equivalent to defining GANTRY_SUPPRESS_GEOMETRY_WARNING in C.

endmenu
